.7}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.92, "name": "Soil microbes and beetles", "desc": "Slowly break down dead plants and animals in dry soil and return nutrients to it."}, {"id": "creosote", "sp": "larrea tridentata", "xh": 0.06, "wiki": "Creosote bush", "desc": "A resinous, drought-hardy shrub that dominates much of the lower desert. Its seeds feed small rodents and its leaves feed some lizards.", "ic": "sage", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "bursage", "sp": "ambrosia dumosa", "xh": 0.22}, {"id": "brittle", "sp": "encelia farinosa", "xh": 0.38}, {"id": "flowers", "sp": "chylismia", "xh": 0.6}, {"id": "cactus", "sp": "opuntia basilaris", "xh": 0.82, "name": "Beavertail cactus", "ic": "sage"}, {"id": "bighorn", "sp": "ovis canadensis nelsoni", "xh": 0.05}, {"id": "kroo", "sp": "dipodomys deserti", "xh": 0.17}, {"id": "squirrel", "sp": "ammospermophilus leucurus", "xh": 0.29, "desc": "A daytime ground squirrel that stays active in desert heat and feeds on seeds, cactus and other items."}, {"id": "jack", "sp": "lepus californicus", "xh": 0.41, "desc": "A nocturnal hare whose big ears shed heat. It is prey for coyotes, as NPS notes.", "ic": "vole"}, {"id": "chuck", "sp": "sauromalus ater", "xh": 0.53}, {"id": "moth", "sp": "hyles lineata", "xh": 0.7, "name": "White-lined sphinx moth", "wiki": "White-lined sphinx", "ic": "mayfly"}, {"id": "uta", "sp": "uta stansburiana", "xh": 0.1}, {"id": "lizard", "sp": "gambelia wislizenii", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "sidewinder", "sp": "crotalus cerastes", "xh": 0.55}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.82, "desc": "An omnivorous scavenger and the most recorded bird in the area. Mojave ravens have boomed around towns and garbage, and prey on young desert tortoises."}, {"id": "coyote", "sp": "canis latrans", "xh": 0.2, "wiki": "Coyote", "desc": "A widespread predator that NPS says hunts mainly at night and in the cool of early morning. Eats rodents, hares, lizards and carrion."}, {"id": "hawk", "sp":